# SEO impact run reports — server-authoritative (cron owns them) and never tracked, but
# a local `node agents/seo-impact/index.js` writes here and they showed up as untracked
# files waiting for someone's `git add .`
data/reports/seo-impact/

# CTR-program wave plans — same reasoning as seo-impact above: cron owns them on
# the server, they are rebuilt from GSC snapshots (which are themselves
# server-authoritative and gitignored), and a committed wave.json would be a
# stale holdout list that meta-optimizer reads as current — which is worse than
# no wave at all, because the holdout it protects would be last month's.
data/reports/ctr-program/

# Long-title remediation run records — server-authoritative machine output, and
# each one embeds every live BEFORE value, so a tracked copy would be both a
# deploy-revert hazard (the class PR #825 removed) and a growing blob of
# duplicated live copy. The record IS the backup; it belongs on the box.
data/reports/long-title-remediation/

# Queue auto-apply run reports — same reasoning as seo-impact above: cron owns
# them on the server, and a local dry run would otherwise leave untracked files
# behind for someone's `git add .`
data/reports/queue-autoapply/

# Agent `latest.json` run reports — server-authoritative, and TRACKING THEM IS AN
# ACTIVE HAZARD, not just untidiness. These 13 were tracked until 2026-09-06.
# Every one is rewritten on the production box; a tracked copy means a deploy can
# revert live data to whatever was last committed, and git can text-merge a
# machine-written JSON file into conflict markers that every reader `catch {}`s
# as "no data". That is the same defect class as `data/rejected-keywords.json`
# and `data/posts/*/meta.json`, and on 2026-09-06 it fired: a `git stash push`
# during a deploy was never popped, and `data/reports/quick-wins/latest.json`
# sat at its 2026-04-14 committed value — `candidate_count: 1` — for 145 days
# while `quick-win-targeter` ran cleanly every Monday and wrote a dated .md
# beside it. Seven agents read that file, so the biggest CTR opportunity on the
# site (the tattoo-soap winner, 43,827 impressions at 0.5% CTR) was invisible to
# the quick-win pool for five months. `gsc-opportunity/latest.json` had the same
# disease but self-healed daily at 13:30 UTC — which is AFTER `daily-summary`
# reads it at 13:00, so the digest reported April data every morning.
#
# These are regenerable machine output, which is what separates them from
# `data/rejected-keywords.json` (human decisions, not regenerable, stays tracked
# and reconciled by union) and `data/briefs/_dropped/` (an archive whose whole
# point is that an untracked copy is what made the original loss unrecoverable).
# Their siblings — health-claim-remediation, antiperspirant-remediation,
# pagespeed, cannibalization, theme-seo-audit — were already untracked; these 13
# were the anomaly. Pinned by tests/repo/server-reports-untracked.test.js.
data/reports/bing-keyword-gap/latest.json
data/reports/claim-audit/latest.json
data/reports/competitor-watcher/latest.json
data/reports/device-weights/latest.json
data/reports/dropship-copy-remediation/latest.json
data/reports/gsc-opportunity/latest.json
data/reports/hero-product/latest.json
data/reports/indexing/latest.json
data/reports/post-performance/latest.json
data/reports/quick-wins/latest.json
data/reports/return-policy-statement/latest.json
data/reports/shopping-test-monitor/latest.json
data/reports/voice-of-customer/latest.json

# Ad Studio run output — one default run writes ~137 MB of 2K renders (a single
# variation is ~7.6 MB × 6 platform targets). Regenerable and reviewed as images, never
# in a diff. Scoped to the ad-studio subtree so the already-tracked data/creatives/
# session-* masters are untouched. There is no retention policy yet: prune old run
# directories by hand — a full disk has already cost this project four days of cron.
data/creatives/ad-studio/

# Ad Studio score baseline — accumulates per environment from real runs, like the run
# output it summarises. Committing it would merge one machine's test runs into another's
# baseline, which is exactly the number it exists to keep honest.
data/reports/ad-studio/

# Per-run LLM spend telemetry, written by lib/llm-meter on every agent run.
# Machine-generated and append-only; scripts/llm-cost.mjs reads it locally.
data/reports/llm-usage/

# Ad Studio brief store — generated output. Scoped to the ad-studio subtree only:
# data/briefs/ itself already holds committed content-brief JSON for a different
# pipeline, and ignoring the parent would silently drop tracked files from future diffs.
data/briefs/ad-studio/

# data/briefs/_dropped/ is deliberately NOT ignored. It holds content briefs that
# scripts/triage-orphan-briefs.mjs took out of circulation, and archiving a tracked
# brief there is a rename git can follow and undo. Ignoring it would make the archive
# itself untracked — which is exactly the condition that made the 2026-08-19 loss of
# vegan-soap/oatmeal-soap/coconut-oil-soap-benefits unrecoverable. See lib/brief-archive.js.

# content-mirror live-body snapshots — read-only captures of what is on Shopify,
# written by scripts/check-content-mirrors.mjs --snapshot-live --apply purely so a
# human can diff them against the local mirror. Regenerable from Shopify, and a
# tracked copy would be one more stale body somebody later mistakes for current.
data/reports/content-mirror/

# Rendered previews of the frustration segment emails. GENERATED from
# lib/giveaway/frustration-campaigns.js, which is the source of truth — committing the
# output would conflict on every concurrent PR and let git 3-way-merge it into copy the
# renderer would never emit (same reason data/context/marketing-tactics.md is ignored).
data/giveaway/frustration/

# Live-theme template backups written by scripts/add-complete-the-routine.mjs.
# Point-in-time copies of a server-authoritative artifact; the theme is the truth.
data/reports/theme-backups/

# Klaviyo flow-push run records and live-body backups — machine-written, and the
# backups are copies of live email HTML that do not belong in git.
data/reports/klaviyo-flow-push/
# Same class as the line above: pre-write campaign JSON + live-body backups. Operational
# recovery artifacts, not repo content, and they carry full campaign bodies.
data/reports/campaign-unsub-repair/

# Per-post local safety copies, written before an overwrite by the reconciler, the
# refresh path and the remediation scripts. Regenerable point-in-time captures of a
# body whose truth is live Shopify — the same reasoning as data/reports/content-mirror/.
# NOTE: 13 of these were swept into the index by a broad `git add` before this rule
# existed. They stay tracked deliberately: `git rm --cached` would delete them from the
# production working tree on the next pull, and this repo does not delete backups.
data/posts/*/backups/
data/posts/*/content.backup-*.html

# Machine-written agent run reports, all regenerable and all server-authoritative on
# cron. Same class as the ~30 data/reports/ entries above; these had simply never been
# added, so every one of them sat permanently untracked in `git status`.
data/reports/pr-targets/
data/reports/presale-terms/
data/reports/priority-tuner/
data/reports/publish-drift/
data/reports/rank-alerter/
data/reports/rank-alerts/
data/reports/reviews/
data/reports/rum/
data/reports/seo-opportunities/

# Structured-data coverage measurements written by scripts/audit-schema-coverage.mjs.
# The TOOLING is tracked (lib/schema-audit.js) precisely so this can be re-measured; a
# committed snapshot is a stale reading of the live web that somebody later quotes as
# current, which is the hazard CLAUDE.md names when it says to re-count rather than
# carry a schema figure forward. Same reasoning as data/reports/content-mirror/.
data/reports/schema-audit/

# The SERVER-OWNED half of a post's metadata. data/posts/<slug>/meta.json used to
# hold both the ~6 authored fields and the ~51 a machine observes or stamps, in one
# file that was tracked in git AND rewritten continuously by cron — and on
# 2026-08-23 that collision fired twice in one day, both times leaving INVALID JSON
# on production, because `git stash pop` runs a line-based TEXT merge over a
# pretty-printed object. Splitting the machine half out and ignoring it is what
# makes the collision structurally impossible; lib/post-meta-reconcile.js was only
# ever the patch.
#
# IT HAS NO REDUNDANCY IN GIT, SO IT IS BACKED UP OFFSITE INSTEAD.
# scripts/backup-snapshots-offsite.sh archives it weekly to DigitalOcean Spaces
# under the `post-state` prefix. That is not optional housekeeping: state.json
# holds shopify_article_id, the only link between a local post directory and its
# live article, plus legacy_locked, indexing_state and published_at across ~200
# posts. Never gitignore this without that backup running.
data/posts/*/state.json

# Pre-write backups from scripts/split-post-meta.mjs — machine-written, and a
# tracked copy of a meta.json would recreate the exact hazard the split removes.
data/reports/post-meta-split/

# Pre-write copies of live theme templates, written by
# scripts/build-product-templates.mjs. Redundant with git history --
# theme/templates/*.json is tracked, so every prior version is already
# recoverable. (Unlike data/briefs/_dropped/, which holds paid work that
# exists nowhere else and is deliberately tracked.)
data/template-backup/

# Culina PPC audit — a raw SP-API finance cache (order-level money) plus the
# generated report. Regenerable, never reviewed as a diff, and the cache holds
# financial line items that have no business in git.
data/reports/culina-ppc/
